# BUFFER-FRESHNESS TEST — single variable off long-20M-v2: buffer_size 10M -> 1M (upstream's value)
#   supervisor.py --queue scripts/tdmpc/buffer_queue.jsonl --run_tag buf --grade_plant baseline
#     --grade_horizon 6 --grade_warm_start --no_early_stop --max_env_steps 10000000
#
# WHAT long-20M-v2 SHOWED (stopped at 5.68M, 2026-08-16). It plateaued and then regressed:
#     slope per 1M      1-2M     2-3M     3-4M     4-5M   4.6-5.7M
#     ground_speed    +0.046   +0.026   +0.002   +0.005    -0.014
#     falls/min       -0.379   -0.266   -0.148   -0.100    +0.133
#   peak speed 0.327 @ 4.65M -> 0.308 (z -3.8); peak return 15.17 @ 4.69M -> 14.20 (z -19.5).
#   Every loss flat (consistency 0.0002, reward 0.115) and gradients down to 0.01 -- the model had
#   stopped learning -- while value_loss ROSE monotonically 0.190 -> 0.216. Grading the 4.65M peak:
#   falls 12.5% of episodes, IDENTICAL to h6-flat at 3M, with worse tilt (8.3 vs 6.5) and worse
#   overshoot (1.40x vs 1.23x). 1.65M extra steps bought no safety at all, only speed.
#
# HYPOTHESIS. buffer_size 10M meant NOTHING WAS EVER EVICTED: at 5.7M a batch was drawn uniformly
